cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this toolkit, please cite it as below."
title: "vmbdiet: a diet - vaginal microbiome association toolkit"
abstract: >-
  A tested, reusable toolkit that standardizes diet - vaginal-microbiome
  association analysis: vaginal community state type (CST) classification
  (dominant-taxon and VALENCIA nearest-centroid / Yue-Clayton) and
  covariate-adjusted association of dietary intake with CST, bacterial
  vaginosis, and Lactobacillus dominance (per-SD adjusted logistic regression
  with Benjamini-Hochberg FDR, Spearman nutrient-taxon correlation,
  Mann-Whitney, and PERMANOVA). Validated end-to-end on two independent public
  cohorts reprocessed from raw 16S reads (PRJNA1188525; PRJNA915128).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jean
    family-names: Yu
    email: jyu9675@gmail.com
keywords:
  - vaginal microbiome
  - diet
  - nutrition
  - bacterial vaginosis
  - community state type
  - VALENCIA
  - Lactobacillus
  - 16S rRNA
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jyu9675/vmbdiet"
